WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.877
I'm Jordy Nelson, and this is "Build Your Squad."

00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:09.259
All right, so my first pick, man...

00:00:11.094 --> 00:00:13.555
is the foundation of the team with the quarterbacks.

00:00:13.555 --> 00:00:16.808
Aaron's not up there, so it makes it a little difficult. That'd been the easy No. 1 pick.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.144
You see Favre, another Packer.

00:00:19.144 --> 00:00:23.023
Since we're here at Super Bowl LIV, Chiefs-49ers,

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:25.859
let's go with—they're callin' it the Montana Bowl, right?

00:00:26.443 --> 00:00:29.279
Ya know, since he played for both. Grew up watchin' Joe when he came over

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:30.238
and played with the Chiefs, so,

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.032
put Joe Montana out there.

00:00:33.158 --> 00:00:34.159
The running back's easy for me.

00:00:35.994 --> 00:00:36.995
Some guy who can do it all,

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:41.041
another Kansan—a lotta people don't realize it, but another Kansan.

00:00:41.291 --> 00:00:42.709
You gotta go with Barry Sanders.

00:00:43.126 --> 00:00:46.296
Grew up in Wichita, Kansas. I grew up in Kansas. So we gotta stick together.

00:00:47.088 --> 00:00:48.089
As receivers...

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:49.883
man.

00:00:51.092 --> 00:00:52.093
This is gonna be—this is tough.

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:56.097
We'll stick with receivers. We'll leave the tight end out. We'll go with Jerry Rice.

00:00:56.806 --> 00:00:59.225
Kind of a given. Um, he's got all the numbers.

00:00:59.768 --> 00:01:01.561
Did it for years and years and years, so,

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:04.773
uh, we'll put him up there, and you gotta keep the chemistry goin'.

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:06.274
You don't wanna mess up the chemistry.

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:09.027
I know a lot about—I had a lot of chemistry with my quarterbacks, so,

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:10.403
you gotta keep the chemistry.

00:01:11.863 --> 00:01:12.739
DBs.

00:01:13.865 --> 00:01:14.866
I loved Ed Reed.

00:01:15.992 --> 00:01:20.580
Just a playmaker, all over the place. Uh, can do it all, leader on a team.

00:01:21.289 --> 00:01:22.457
Played with an incredible defense.

00:01:23.792 --> 00:01:24.793
And someone...

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:27.378
we'll go Reggie White to get after the quarterback.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:31.257
Put another—get a Packer guy in there. I know he's in an Eagles uniform but,

00:01:31.633 --> 00:01:33.718
um, kinda changed the Packer organization.

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:37.514
Put 'em back on the map with the Super Bowl, with him and Brett comin' in, so.

00:01:38.056 --> 00:01:40.850
There you go, there's my squad. I don't think you can argue with it.

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:44.062
Obviously, talk about the quarterback; it was difficult. Obviously, these guys are all great.

00:01:44.479 --> 00:01:46.397
Winners. Productive. Everything.

00:01:46.689 --> 00:01:49.609
I would've thrown 12 in there for my, for my sake.

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.486
Running backs is easy for me just with Barry.

00:01:53.029 --> 00:01:54.614
The pass-catchers is tough.

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:58.576
I mean, you got Randy, who had a long career and did it in multiple spots

00:01:58.743 --> 00:02:03.206
and did it at an elite level, especially early on too, and then came back with New England.

00:02:04.165 --> 00:02:07.085
Tony Gonzalez is probably one of the most steady guys out there,

00:02:07.085 --> 00:02:11.131
so that was tough not to, not to pick him. But you gotta—I had to go with a receiver, so.

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:14.175
In the DB world, Deion is the guy, but I wanted to go with a safety,

00:02:14.175 --> 00:02:16.136
with Ed and all the playmaking he did, but

00:02:16.678 --> 00:02:21.599
Deion would've—shoot, I coulda had Deion play receiver and DB and return punts.

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:24.102
So, probably shoulda done that. Coulda gotten more out of one guy.

00:02:25.019 --> 00:02:27.438
And then Reggie was a given, so, we'll go with that one.

00:02:27.438 --> 00:02:28.982
All right, so this is my squad right here.

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:31.526
We got Joe Montana throwin' to his guy Jerry Rice,

00:02:31.526 --> 00:02:34.737
who's gonna be open all the time cuz they're worried about Barry Sanders runnin' the ball.

00:02:34.737 --> 00:02:36.322
And then we have the stoppers on defense,

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:39.450
the guy gettin' after the quarterback and the guy pickin' off all the passes.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.327
So, this is my squad.

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:43.121
On behalf of Michelob Ultra Pure Gold,

00:02:43.121 --> 00:02:46.416
the organic beer changing regular farms into organic farms.

